BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Playing With the World: How Games Have Shaped Modern Science and T
 echnology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T193000
UID:playing-with-the-world-how-games-have-shaped-modern-science-and-techno
 logy-2026-06-04t18-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/05
 /Reunion-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:From Neolithic times to the present\, humans around the world 
 have played games. Join Dr. Samuel Pizelo\, Assistant Professor at the Uni
 versity of Toronto\, as he discusses the immense and ongoing influence the
 se games have had on the development of science and technology — from ge
 ometry and statistics to computing\, artificial intelligence\, and the com
 plexity sciences.\n\nBy focusing on the role of traditional games like che
 ss and backgammon in these developments\, we can understand science and te
 chnology not as a series of individual discoveries\, but as a shared globa
 l heritage.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/playing-with-the-world/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
